<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#counterweight-trebuchet">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Counterweight trebuchet</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as counterweight trebuchets</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A counterweight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trebuchet">trebuchet</a> is a siege engine that uses a heavy falling weight to swing a throwing arm, capable of hurling large stones over long distances. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-xiangyang">siege of Xiangyang</a>, Persian engineers introduced counterweight trebuchets that outranged Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catapult">catapults</a>. The weapon helped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> break <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> defences.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/counterweight-trebuchet.jpg" alt="Counterweight trebuchet" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quistnix · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trebuchet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
